  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 17,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.645,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Peek Beyond the Point"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.199
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus decimal notation is a natural extension of the Indian place value system to numbers also having fractional parts. Just as 705 means "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 \\times 1 0 0 \\div 5 \\times 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , the number 70.5 means "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 \\times 1 0 \\pm 5 \\times \\frac { 1 } { 1 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and 7.05 means "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 \\times 1 \\div 5 \\times \\frac { 1 } { 1 0 0 } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.203,
            0.848,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen how to write numbers using the decimal point (‘.’). But how do we read/say these numbers?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.251,
            0.713,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that 705 is read as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "seven hundred and five",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.27,
            0.847,
            0.325
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "70.5 is read as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "seventy point five",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", short for "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "seventy and five-tenths",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". 7.05 is read as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "seven point zero five",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", short for "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "seven and five hundredths",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.325,
            0.848,
            0.381
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "0.274 is read as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "zero point two seven four",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". We don’t read it as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "zero point two hundred and seventy four",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as 0.274 means "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2 one-tenths and 7 one-hundredths and 4 one-thousandths",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.39,
            0.846,
            0.43
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Make a place value table similar to the one above. Write each quantity in decimal form and in terms of place value, and read the number:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.445,
            0.57,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) 2 ones, 3 tenths and 5 hundredths"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.469,
            0.412,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) 1 ten and 5 tenths"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.493,
            0.48,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) 4 ones and 6 hundredths"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.517,
            0.574,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(d) 1 hundred, 1 one and 1 hundredth"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.543,
            0.344,
            0.579
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(e) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{8}{100}  and  \\frac{9}{10}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.584,
            0.271,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(f) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 5 } { 1 0 0 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.625,
            0.26,
            0.66
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(g) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 1 0 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.664,
            0.458,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(h) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2\\frac{1}{100},4\\frac{1}{10}\\bmod7\\frac{7}{1000}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.703,
            0.846,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the chapter on large numbers, we learned how to write 23 hundreds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.74,
            0.607,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "23 hundred "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "s = 23 \\times 100 = 2000 + 300 = 2300."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.769,
            0.843,
            0.852
          ],
          "content": [
            {
